data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261017194711160105501c955d568LWdhUW6o","created":1792266431,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7c93d69eb437405182d88206","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"content\":\"Formal Specification of sort_list\\n=================================\\n\\nNotation\\n--------\\n|L|            : length of list L\\nL[i]           : element of L at index i (0-based, defined for 0 <= i < |L|)\\nocc(x, L)      : number of occurrences of element x in L\\n                 occ(x, L) = |{ i : 0 <= i < |L| and L[i] = x }|\\n<=_Z           : the usual non-decreasing order on integers\\n\\n\\nFirst-Order Logic Formulation\\n-----------------------------\\n\\nPredicate definitions:\\n\\n  Sorted(M)  =def  forall i. (0 <= i < |M| - 1  ->  M[i] <= M[i+1])\\n\\n  Perm(L, M) =def  forall x. (occ(x, L) = occ(x, M))\\n\\n    (i.e., L and M have exactly the same elements with the same\\n     multiplicities -- multiset equality)\\n\\nMain theorem (the specification):\\n\\n  forall L.  Sorted(sort_list(L))  and  Perm(L, sort_list(L))\\n\\nEquivalently, using a global-index sortedness condition\\n(provable to be equivalent to the adjacent-pair version for lists\\nover a total order):\\n\\n  forall L.  ( forall i, j. (0 <= i <= j < |sort_list(L)|\\n                              ->  sort_list(L)[i] <= sort_list(L)[j]) )\\n             and\\n             ( forall x. occ(x, L) = occ(x, sort_list(L)) )\\n\\n\\nProof-Assistant Formulation (Lean 4 style)\\n------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef Sorted (l : List Int) : Prop :=\\n  forall i j, 0 <= i -> i <= j -> j < l.length -> l[i]! <= l[j]!\\n\\ndef Perm (l m : List Int) : Prop :=\\n  forall x, l.count x = m.count x\\n\\ntheorem sort_list_spec (L : List Int) :\\n    Sorted (sort_list L) /\\\\ Perm L (sort_list L)\\n\\n\\nProof-Assistant Formulation (Coq style)\\n---------------------------------------\\n\\nDefinition Sorted (m : list Z) : Prop :=\\n  forall i j, i <= j -> j < length m -> nth i m 0 <=? nth j m 0 = true.\\n\\nDefinition Perm (l m : list Z) : Prop :=\\n  forall x, count_occ x l = count_occ x m.\\n\\nTheorem sort_list_spec : forall L : list Z,\\n  Sorted (sort_list L) /\\\\ Perm L (sort_list L).\\n\",\"path\":\"sorting_verification/formal_spec.txt\"}"}}]}}]}

