data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261017194913367341857c955d568bA6aHKs1","created":1792266553,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_f9bb8d14281f424e8dadd194","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"content\":\"Proof Obligations for sort_list (insertion sort)\\n================================================\\n\\nImplementation recap\\n--------------------\\n  def sort_list(items):\\n      result = list(items)                    # O1 concerns this copy\\n      for i in range(1, len(result)):         # outer loop over i\\n          key = result[i]\\n          j = i - 1\\n          while j >= 0 and result[j] > key:   # inner shift loop\\n              result[j + 1] = result[j]\\n              j -= 1\\n          result[j + 1] = key\\n      return result\\n\\nGoal (from formal_spec.txt):\\n  forall L. Sorted(sort_list(L)) and Perm(L, sort_list(L))\\n\\nWe prove the stronger inductive statement by proving the obligations\\nbelow; the final theorem follows by taking the state at loop exit.\\n\\n\\nObligation 1 -- Copy yields a permutation (base permutation fact)\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\n  O1: forall L. Perm(L, copy(L))\\n      where copy(L) is the list produced by `result = list(items)`.\\n\\n  Proof idea: copy is an elementwise copy; occ(x, copy(L)) = occ(x, L)\\n  for every x, by induction on the length of L (appending preserves\\n  occurrence counts).\\n\\n\\nObligation 2 -- Outer loop preserves permutation (permutation preservation)\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  O2: If Perm(L, result) holds before one outer-loop iteration (state\\n      for index i), and the iteration transforms result into result'\\n      (inner shift loop plus key placement), then Perm(L, result')\\n      holds after the iteration.\\n\\n  Sub-obligation 2a -- inner shift preserves permutation:\\n    O2a: If Perm(L, M) and M' is obtained from M by setting\\n         M'[j+1] = M[j] (right shift) for a fixed j, then Perm(L, M').\\n    Proof idea: the multiset of M' equals the multiset of M because\\n    the shifted element is duplicated then overwritten; more precisely\\n    occ(x, M') = occ(x, M) for all x, by case analysis on the positions\\n    j, j+1 and all other positions (which are unchanged).\\n\\n  Sub-obligation 2b -- key placement preserves permutation:\\n    O2b: If Perm(L, M) holds for the state after the inner loop, and\\n         result' is obtained by result'[j+1] = key where key was the\\n         value removed from position i at the start of the iteration\\n         (result[i] = key, and positions i+1.. are untouched, position\\n         i is overwritten by the shift), then Perm(L, result').\\n    Proof idea: over the whole iteration, the multiset of the segment\\n    [0..i] is unchanged: the key is taken out of the multiset and put\\n    back exactly once; all other writes are the shifts of O2a.\\n\\n  Together O1 + O2 (iterated over all outer iterations) give:\\n    Perm(L, sort_list(L)).\\n\\n\\nObligation 3 -- Inner loop invariant (shift-loop correctness)\\n-------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Invariant INV_inner at the start of each inner-loop iteration\\n  (state with current j), assuming the state at the start of the\\n  outer iteration i had:\\n    P1: result[0..i-1] is sorted (non-decreasing)\\n    P2: key = the original result[i] (value saved before shifting)\\n    P3: result[i] currently holds the value of result[i-1] (already\\n        shifted) or key is still in place if no shift has happened\\n\\n  INV_inner: after the shift result[j+1] = result[j] and decrement,\\n  the list still satisfies Perm (by O2a) and:\\n    INV1: result[0..j] is sorted and all elements of result[0..j]\\n          are <= key  (so the loop guard result[j] > key is exactly\\n          the condition to keep shifting)\\n    INV2: result[j+2..i] are all equal to key (they are copies of the\\n          shifted values), so the multiset is preserved.\\n\\n  Termination (variant): the natural number j decreases by 1 each\\n  iteration and is bounded below by -1, so the inner loop terminates.\\n    O3-term: j is a termination measure for the inner loop.\\n\\n\\nObligation 4 -- Outer loop invariant (partial sortedness)\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n  Invariant INV_outer before each outer iteration with index i:\\n    INV3: result[0..i-1] is sorted (non-decreasing)\\n    INV4: Perm(L, result)  (carried from O1/O2)\\n\\n  Base case: i = 1; result[0..0] is a single element, trivially sorted\\n  (base case of the induction).\\n\\n  Inductive step: assuming INV3 and INV4 for i, after the iteration\\n  (inner shift loop + key placement) the list satisfies INV3 for i+1:\\n  result[0..i] is sorted.\\n    Proof idea: by the inner-loop invariant, the shift loop stops at\\n    the first position j with result[j] <= key (or at j = -1); the key\\n    is placed at j+1; elements left of j+1 are <= key (INV1), elements\\n    right of j+1 up to i are >= key (they are >= key by the guard\\n    condition), and result[i+1..] were already >= all of result[0..i]\\n    by the previous invariant; hence result[0..i] is sorted.\\n\\n  This is the inductive step of the main induction on i.\\n\\n\\nObligation 5 -- Sortedness of the final result\\n----------------------------------------------\\n  O5: At loop exit (i = |result| = |L|), INV3 gives\\n        result[0..|L|-1] is sorted,\\n      which is exactly Sorted(sort_list(L)) (adjacent-pair form).\\n  Combined with INV4 (Perm(L, result)) we obtain the goal:\\n        Sorted(sort_list(L)) and Perm(L, sort_list(L)).\\n\\n\\nObligation 6 -- Termination of the outer loop\\n---------------------------------------------\\n  O6: i ranges over 1..|result|, increasing by 1 each iteration, and\\n  |result| is fixed by the copy step, so the outer loop terminates.\\n  (Needed so that sort_list actually returns a value and O5 applies\\n  to the returned list.)\\n\\n\\nSummary of the proof structure\\n------------------------------\\n  O1 (copy permutes)                 -> Perm base\\n  O2a, O2b (iteration preserves Perm) -> Perm induction\\n  O3   (inner invariant + variant)    -> inner loop soundness & termination\\n  O4   (outer invariant)              -> sortedness induction\\n                                          (base: single element; step: O4)\\n  O5   (exit condition)               -> final theorem\\n  O6   (outer variant)                -> overall termination\\n\",\"path\":\"sorting_verification/obligations.txt\"}"}}]}}]}

