data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261017195330752627318c955d568WaAkXOTY","created":1792266811,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_246a3a99b6834d318ec4525e","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"content\":\"Proof Obligations for sort_list (insertion sort)\\n================================================\\n\\nImplementation recap\\n--------------------\\n  def sort_list(items):\\n      result = list(items)                    # copy; OB1 concerns this\\n      for i in range(1, len(result)):         # outer loop, i = 1..n-1\\n          key = result[i]                     # key held OUT of the array\\n          j = i - 1\\n          while j >= 0 and result[j] > key:   # inner shift loop\\n              result[j + 1] = result[j]\\n              j -= 1\\n          result[j + 1] = key                 # key written back: Perm restored\\n      return result\\n\\nGoal (from formal_spec.txt):\\n  forall L. Sorted(sort_list(L)) and Perm(L, sort_list(L))\\n\\nNotation: |L| = n. a_0..a_{n-1} are the elements of the input L.\\nb_0..b_{i-1} denote result[0..i-1] at the START of outer iteration i\\n(the current prefix, which is sorted by INV-OUT.B but need not be in\\noriginal input order after earlier iterations). \\\"sorted(s, e)\\\" means\\nresult[s..e] is non-decreasing. occ(x, M) is the number of occurrences\\nof x in M, and multiset(M) is the multiset of M's elements.\\n\\n\\nLoop invariants\\n---------------\\nINV-OUT(i)  (before outer iteration i, 1 <= i <= n):\\n  (A) Perm(L, result)               -- occ(x, result) = occ(x, L) for all x\\n  (B) sorted(0, i-1)                -- prefix of length i is sorted\\n  (C) result[p] = a_p for all p >= i -- suffix untouched so far\\n\\nINV-IN(j)  (at the inner-loop guard, during outer iteration i,\\n            with key = a_i saved before any shift):\\n  (1) multiset(result) = multiset(L) - {key} + {result[j+1]}\\n        -- \\\"hole accounting\\\": key is held out; position j+1 is the\\n           hole, currently holding the most recently shifted value\\n           (or key itself, if no shift has happened yet, j+1 = i)\\n  (2) result[0..j] = b_0..b_j  and  sorted(0, j)\\n  (3) result[j+2..i] = b_{j+1}..b_{i-1}  (the displaced prefix elements,\\n        still in their original relative order), hence sorted(j+2, i)\\n        and every one of them > key\\n  (4) result[p] = a_p for all p >= i+1\\n\\n\\nObligations\\n-----------\\n\\nOB1  (Copy yields a permutation -- base permutation fact)\\n  After `result = list(items)`:\\n    Perm(L, result)  and  result[p] = a_p for all 0 <= p < n.\\n  Proof: elementwise copy; occ(x, copy(L)) = occ(x, L) for all x.\\n\\nOB2  (Inner invariant establishment)\\n  At the start of outer iteration i (1 <= i < n), from INV-OUT(i)\\n  and key = result[i] = a_i, j = i-1: INV-IN(i-1) holds.\\n  Checks: (1) the hole is position i, holding key itself, so\\n  multiset(result) = multiset(L) - {key} + {key} = multiset(L);\\n  (2) positions 0..j are untouched since iteration start, so\\n  result[0..j] = b_0..b_{i-1}, sorted by INV-OUT(i).B; (3) the range\\n  j+2..i is empty; (4) suffix by INV-OUT(i).C.\\n\\nOB3  (Inner invariant preservation -- shift step)\\n  If INV-IN(j) and the guard holds (j >= 0 and result[j] > key),\\n  then after `result[j+1] = result[j]; j -= 1`, INV-IN(j-1) holds.\\n  Proof sketch:\\n    - (1): the write replaces the hole content b_{j+1} (duplicated\\n      one slot up) by b_j; the new hole is at (j-1)+1 = j. Both the\\n      old and new right-hand sides change by -{b_{j+1}} + {b_j}.\\n    - (2): positions 0..j-1 untouched, still b_0..b_{j-1}, sorted\\n      because the prefix b was sorted at iteration start.\\n    - (3): the displaced region is now result[j+1..i] = b_j followed\\n      by the old b_{j+1}..b_{i-1}; it is sorted since b_j <= b_{j+1}\\n      (original prefix sorted), and b_j > key by the guard.\\n    - (4): untouched.\\n  Termination (variant): j strictly decreases and is bounded below\\n  by -1 (the guard requires j >= 0), so the inner loop terminates.\\n\\nOB4  (Inner exit -- key placement restores Perm and extends sortedness)\\n  If INV-IN(j) and the guard fails (j < 0 or result[j] <= key), then\\n  after `result[j+1] = key`, INV-OUT(i+1) holds:\\n    - (A) Perm: by (1), multiset(result) = multiset(L) - {key} +\\n      {result[j+1]}; the write replaces that hole value by key,\\n      restoring exactly multiset(L).\\n    - (B) sorted(0, i): head result[0..j] = b_0..b_j is sorted with\\n      all elements <= key (at exit result[j] <= key, and the head is\\n      sorted; empty when j < 0); key sits at j+1; the tail\\n      result[j+2..i] is sorted with all elements > key by (3).\\n      Edge case j+1 = i (no shift occurred): the write is a no-op and\\n      sortedness of 0..i follows from the failed guard alone\\n      (result[i-1] <= key, prefix sorted).\\n    - (C) suffix: shifts and the write only touch positions <= i.\\n  This obligation discharges permutation preservation (with OB1, OB3)\\n  and the inductive step for sortedness.\\n\\nOB5  (Outer base case)\\n  INV-OUT(1) holds on loop entry: (A) and (C) by OB1; (B) sorted(0,0)\\n  is trivial (single element). Degenerate inputs n <= 1 never enter\\n  the loop, and OB1 + trivial sortedness give the postcondition\\n  directly.\\n\\nOB6  (Outer inductive step)\\n  For 1 <= i < n: INV-OUT(i) implies INV-OUT(i+1).\\n  Proof: OB2 establishes INV-IN, OB3 preserves it around the inner\\n  loop, OB4 closes the iteration. This is the main induction on i.\\n\\nOB7  (Postcondition at outer exit)\\n  At loop exit i = n: INV-OUT(n) gives sorted(0, n-1), i.e.\\n  Sorted(sort_list(L)), and Perm(L, result), i.e.\\n  Perm(L, sort_list(L)). Together with OB5 this proves the goal.\\n\\nOB8  (Termination)\\n  Outer variant: n - i strictly decreases each iteration and is\\n  bounded below by 0, so the outer loop terminates and sort_list\\n  returns (needed for OB7 to apply to the returned list).\\n\\n\\nSummary of the proof structure\\n------------------------------\\n  OB1  copy permutes                  -> Perm base\\n  OB2  inner invariants established   -> links outer/inner loops\\n  OB3  shift preserves invariants     -> inner inductive step (+ inner\\n                                          termination variant)\\n  OB4  exit restores Perm, extends sorted prefix\\n                                      -> permutation preservation and\\n                                         sortedness inductive step\\n  OB5  base case i = 1                -> sortedness base case\\n  OB6  outer inductive step           -> INV-OUT(i) for all i\\n  OB7  postcondition                  -> final theorem\\n  OB8  outer termination              -> totality of sort_list\\n\",\"path\":\"sorting_verification/obligations.txt\"}"}}]}}]}

